Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Karl and fellow Rqtl-ers,
I would like to do some marker regressions and I was wondering if there was any straightforward way of getting all of the regression statistics out from the analysis, and not just the LOD scores (slopes and intercepts).  I may just write a function to do all of the regressions, but I thought I would check to see if there would be any quick way to do it using scanone and method 'mr'.

Thanks,
Kevin

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Mon Nov 21 18:11:23 2011
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Mon, 21 Nov 2011 18:11:23 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] marker regression data
Message-ID: <V1_OBOfYIec.XEb2ulXFnjcJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <V1_OBOfYIec.RZzhGMQHjJQJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <V1_OBOfYIec.RZzhGMQHjJQJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/V1_OBOfYIec/m/XEb2ulXFnjcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No; at present, scanone only provides LOD scores.  Estimated effects can only be obtained through fitqtl.   The effectscan function might work, too.

karl

